{"document":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"heading","depth":1,"id":"react-api","children":[{"type":"text","value":"React API"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"@tanstack/highlight/react"},{"type":"text","value":" prepares code-block data for React components. It intentionally does not import React, render elements, own copy state, or inject CSS."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"createhighlightedcodeblockpropsoptions","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"CreateHighlightedCodeBlockPropsOptions"}]},{"type":"code","value":"type CreateHighlightedCodeBlockPropsOptions = {\n  className?: string\n  code: string\n  decorations?: ReadonlyArray<HighlightDecoration>\n  highlighter: Highlighter\n  lang?: string\n  lineNumbers?: boolean\n  title?: string\n}","lang":"ts"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"highlightedcodeblockprops","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"HighlightedCodeBlockProps"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"link","href":"core#renderedcodeblockdata","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"RenderedCodeBlockData"}]},{"type":"text","value":" plus an optional "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"className"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"createhighlightedcodeblockprops","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"createHighlightedCodeBlockProps"}]},{"type":"code","value":"function createHighlightedCodeBlockProps(\n  options: CreateHighlightedCodeBlockPropsOptions,\n): HighlightedCodeBlockProps","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Calls "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"highlighter.renderCodeBlockData"},{"type":"text","value":" and preserves "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"className"},{"type":"text","value":". It is deterministic and produces the same data during SSR and hydration."}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { createHighlightedCodeBlockProps } from '@tanstack/highlight/react'\n\nfunction CodeBlock(input: Omit<CreateHighlightedCodeBlockPropsOptions, 'highlighter'>) {\n  const block = createHighlightedCodeBlockProps({ ...input, highlighter })\n\n  return (\n    <figure className={block.className}>\n      {block.title ? <figcaption>{block.title}</figcaption> : null}\n      <div dangerouslySetInnerHTML={{ __html: block.htmlMarkup }} />\n    </figure>\n  )\n}","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"htmlMarkup"},{"type":"text","value":" is escaped by the library. Do not append unrelated unescaped HTML to it before rendering. See the "},{"type":"link","href":"../guides/react","children":[{"type":"text","value":"React guide"}]},{"type":"text","value":"."}]}],"headings":[{"id":"react-api","text":"React API","level":1},{"id":"createhighlightedcodeblockpropsoptions","text":"CreateHighlightedCodeBlockPropsOptions","level":2},{"id":"highlightedcodeblockprops","text":"HighlightedCodeBlockProps","level":2},{"id":"createhighlightedcodeblockprops","text":"createHighlightedCodeBlockProps","level":2}]},"frameworks":[],"downloadMarkdown":"\n# React API\n\n`@tanstack/highlight/react` prepares code-block data for React components. It intentionally does not import React, render elements, own copy state, or inject CSS.\n\n## `CreateHighlightedCodeBlockPropsOptions`\n\n```ts\ntype CreateHighlightedCodeBlockPropsOptions = {\n  className?: string\n  code: string\n  decorations?: ReadonlyArray<HighlightDecoration>\n  highlighter: Highlighter\n  lang?: string\n  lineNumbers?: boolean\n  title?: string\n}\n```\n\n## `HighlightedCodeBlockProps`\n\n[`RenderedCodeBlockData`](core#renderedcodeblockdata) plus an optional `className`.\n\n## `createHighlightedCodeBlockProps`\n\n```ts\nfunction createHighlightedCodeBlockProps(\n  options: CreateHighlightedCodeBlockPropsOptions,\n): HighlightedCodeBlockProps\n```\n\nCalls `highlighter.renderCodeBlockData` and preserves `className`. It is deterministic and produces the same data during SSR and hydration.\n\n```tsx\nimport { createHighlightedCodeBlockProps } from '@tanstack/highlight/react'\n\nfunction CodeBlock(input: Omit<CreateHighlightedCodeBlockPropsOptions, 'highlighter'>) {\n  const block = createHighlightedCodeBlockProps({ ...input, highlighter })\n\n  return (\n    <figure className={block.className}>\n      {block.title ? <figcaption>{block.title}</figcaption> : null}\n      <div dangerouslySetInnerHTML={{ __html: block.htmlMarkup }} />\n    </figure>\n  )\n}\n```\n\n`htmlMarkup` is escaped by the library. Do not append unrelated unescaped HTML to it before rendering. See the [React guide](../guides/react).\n","originalRawMarkdown":"---\ntitle: React API\n---\n\n# React API\n\n`@tanstack/highlight/react` prepares code-block data for React components. It intentionally does not import React, render elements, own copy state, or inject CSS.\n\n## `CreateHighlightedCodeBlockPropsOptions`\n\n```ts\ntype CreateHighlightedCodeBlockPropsOptions = {\n  className?: string\n  code: string\n  decorations?: ReadonlyArray<HighlightDecoration>\n  highlighter: Highlighter\n  lang?: string\n  lineNumbers?: boolean\n  title?: string\n}\n```\n\n## `HighlightedCodeBlockProps`\n\n[`RenderedCodeBlockData`](core#renderedcodeblockdata) plus an optional `className`.\n\n## `createHighlightedCodeBlockProps`\n\n```ts\nfunction createHighlightedCodeBlockProps(\n  options: CreateHighlightedCodeBlockPropsOptions,\n): HighlightedCodeBlockProps\n```\n\nCalls `highlighter.renderCodeBlockData` and preserves `className`. It is deterministic and produces the same data during SSR and hydration.\n\n```tsx\nimport { createHighlightedCodeBlockProps } from '@tanstack/highlight/react'\n\nfunction CodeBlock(input: Omit<CreateHighlightedCodeBlockPropsOptions, 'highlighter'>) {\n  const block = createHighlightedCodeBlockProps({ ...input, highlighter })\n\n  return (\n    <figure className={block.className}>\n      {block.title ? <figcaption>{block.title}</figcaption> : null}\n      <div dangerouslySetInnerHTML={{ __html: block.htmlMarkup }} />\n    </figure>\n  )\n}\n```\n\n`htmlMarkup` is escaped by the library. Do not append unrelated unescaped HTML to it before rendering. See the [React guide](../guides/react).\n"}
